# The Rust port is authored and generated with LF endings, and its fixtures and
# generated sources are byte-compared against a fresh regeneration. Without this
# rule core.autocrlf rewrites them to CRLF on checkout and the drift checks fail.
rust/** text eol=lf

# The canaries are checked out and built on both hosted Linux and this Windows
# host. They compare formatted output byte for byte, so they get the same rule
# rather than inheriting core.autocrlf and differing by platform.
canaries/** text eol=lf
